course: dictionary
lesson: 16023
title: Vending and vending machines
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Vending» means selling, especially selling things from a machine. You can work it out from the words around it. «Sam put two coins into the vending machine and a bag of crisps dropped out.» Coins and crisps coming out tell you the machine sells things.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. Then try your meaning in the sentence. «Sam put two coins into the selling machine and a bag of crisps dropped out» still makes sense, so selling is a good meaning for vending.
explain: «Vending» is mostly used in the phrase «vending machine». A vending machine gives you a snack, drink or ticket when you put money in. «Street vending» means selling things out on the street.
fact: Vending means selling, especially selling things from a machine.
fact: A vending machine gives you a snack, drink or ticket when you put money in.
fact: Vending is an uncountable noun, so we do not add s to make it plural.
fact: Vending machines are often found at stations, schools and leisure centres.
fact: In maths, vending machine problems help you work with coins and change: a drink costs 80p, you pay £1, and you get 20p change.
exercise: «The vending machine in the corridor sells cold drinks.» What is a vending machine? | A machine that cuts grass | *A machine that sells things when you put money in | A machine that washes clothes | A machine that makes the lights go on
exercise: «Mia bought a cold drink from the vending machine after swimming.» Where did Mia buy her drink? | From the pool's lost property box | From a teacher's desk | *From a machine | At home, from the fridge
exercise: Ben says vending is plural, so we should write vendings. Is he right? | *No, vending is uncountable, so it has no plural | Yes, but only at weekends | Yes, add s to make vendings | No, because vending is a colour
test: «Street vending» is common in busy towns. What does street vending mean? | Building new roads | Cleaning the streets | *Selling things out on the street | Driving cars very fast
test: A vending machine drink costs 75p. Jo pays £1. How much change should she get? | 1p | 75p | 175p | *25p
exam: What does a vending machine do? | Makes the lights go on | *Sells snacks, drinks or tickets when you put money in | Washes clothes | Cuts grass
